  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "1 \u00b7 Ingest and retain source truth",
      "items": [
        "Four merchant/offer connectors: Awin, Admitad, Commission Factory and Kwanko. Transaction sync currently calls Awin and Admitad.",
        "Network + merchant identity keeps feeds separate. Complete feeds can remove stale offers; partial feeds retain last-good data. Manual offers and operator flags are protected.",
        "MongoDB holds advertisers, deals, products, transactions, clicks, alert subscriptions, verifications, permissions and sync metadata. These are application modules inside one Next.js app."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "2 \u00b7 Correct regional publication",
      "items": [
        "Only joined merchants with active status or an editor-selected flagship are eligible. Directory pages include eligible stores with zero offers; offer showcases still require offers.",
        "Offer market priority: reviewed override \u2192 explicit offer markets \u2192 matched merchant geography when the feed omits it. Explicit reviewed [] withholds the offer. Unknown geography does not imply worldwide.",
        "Offer ownership checks network, merchant ID and normalized name. Expired, future, quarantined, generated placeholder and AI-review offers are withheld. Deduplication happens before counts and pagination."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "3 \u00b7 Coupons, deals and products",
      "items": [
        "Any nonblank coupon code belongs to Coupons. A code-free promotion belongs to product Promotions; other code-free records belong to Deals. Store data fetches every result page.",
        "Admin isExclusive survives into public cards and sorts first. Public cards show Exclusive, Source: Merchant and the available update/expiry information.",
        "The products collection is a separate comparison catalog: market/currency filters and identifier-based matching. Product promotions on store pages remain offer records, not automatic catalog imports."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "4 \u00b7 Shopping, revenue and PPC",
      "items": [
        "Offer shopping links use /api/outbound: recheck eligibility, capture attribution, log a click and append the network click identifier before redirecting externally.",
        "At the pinned revision, product comparison buttons use their stored affiliate URLs directly. They do not pass through the store-offer /api/outbound handler.",
        "Affiliate networks report transactions later; revenue is imported and summarized in the dashboard. The diagram does not assume every click becomes an order.",
        "PPC outreach uses SMTP; n8n replies require human review. Launch readiness checks written permission, scope, partnership, offers, tracking and human economics approval. No automatic ad-platform deployment is asserted."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "orange",
      "title": "5 \u00b7 Alerts, cache and optional services",
      "items": [
        "Confirmed store followers receive matching offers in their region; confirmed product subscribers receive emails when the stored current price meets their target and stock checks pass.",
        "Failed email sends retain the notification cursor. SMTP, AI keys and n8n workflows are configuration-dependent capabilities; their production activation is not established by the repository.",
        "Public cache revalidation defaults to 60 seconds with tagged invalidation after admin edits. vercel.json configures feed jobs daily at 03:00 UTC plus alert, outreach and staleness schedules. Actual hosting and job execution remain unverified."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Verified fixes \u00b7 October 9, 2026",
      "items": [
        "Beauty Amora / Commission Factory 83335: 6 public coupons + 10 deals + 0 product promotions. BUFIRST retains its Exclusive flag. The public total matches the store count; its offers do not leak into the US.",
        "Market and ownership fixtures passed for all 37 configured regions. Production build and all 18 test files passed. These checks validate the workspace; no deployment is claimed.",
        "Source links are pinned to commit 88c9618308be. The extra market-audit scripts were uncommitted when this diagram was authored; validation results describe the current workspace."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
